WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
In 1987, researchers handed volunteers a bell.
Their instruction: don't think of a white bear.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Ring if it appears. The bear kept visiting.
But the surprise came afterward.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Some people thought of it more often
once suppression ended.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Later research found the story more complicated.
Rebound is not the same as instant failure.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Newer training studies challenge the rule
that stopping a thought always makes it worse.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
This wasn't a test of meditation audio.
Read the evidence at Final Vestige.
